Hello Nethackers,

The character I asked about earlier finally ascended. Now I just might spend
some
time messing with Putty and that Finnish Tournament server, but I doubt I'll
get
much far. As usual, I'm going to add this YAAP to
http://free.top.bg/kamenk/nethack.htm

This is my sixth ascension and this character was the best prepared for the
end
game. I had 3 cursed ?oGD (fourth is not needed for the Plane of Water), a
=oConflict (for the Plane of Fire), two "oLS and two spare wishes for the
Astral
Plane. Before going for the Wizard I had mapped almost all of Gehennom,
marked the
vibrating square and spent an eternity casting create monster at an altar
just
before Medusa's island. This way I accumulated huge amounts of wands,
potions,
scrolls and what not and for the first time ever the Planes were not
insanely
difficult. This may not seem much, but for me patience is a serious
problem - I'm
sure I couldn't survive an extinctionist game for example.
I usually don't keep notes and I started this game a couple of weeks ago, so
I
don't remember much of the early game. But I remember the most important
thing -
the reason this character ascended is that he found a wand of wishing in a
shop at
Dlvl 3. It was something like 450 gold, so I sold all my spellbooks and
couple of
other items and bought it, since I didn't/couldn't mess with the shopkeeper.
I
wished for a scroll of charging, after that a +2 gray dragon scale mail, got
it at
+2. I visited Minetown (chaotic priest, never killed him) and waited to see
the
last level of Sokoban. It had the amulet of reflection so I wished for a
pair of
speed boots. After Sokoban I went for the end of the Mines. A magic lamp I
found
in Minetown gave me a djin, who remained a pet until something killed him. I
found
another magic lamp, which I used as a light source. At some point I wasted a
wish
for a bag of holding (three or four random one were generated) and for the
Eye of
Aethiopica (sp?), before I realised it was useless. See, lots of artifacts
were
already generated and I didn't remember the Eye was neutral and my
character -
lawful. The bottom level of the Mines was the King's cellar. I had enough
potions
to make holy water by #dipping into my starting ones, without ever
disturbing the
cross-aligned temple priest, exept for donating of course - that's one good
thing
about playing this class. But that also meant I had no artifact weapon until
I

found the only other altar in game, at Dlvl 22 I think. So I used the
starting +1
mace throughout the early game. The first sacrifice session gave me a couple
of
lesser artefacts and I used Sunsword for the Quest.
Forever killed Medusa before the Quest, reverse genocided wraiths to get to
level
14 and went on to retrieve the Mitre of Holiness. Just before Nalzok he got
surrounded by undead and wasted another wish on a ring of conflict - found a
random generated one *on the same freaking level*. The Quest nemesis was
easy,
after Forever cleverly applied the trick with the ?oScare Monster on the
upstairs.
After the Quest a really long sacrifice-on-the-altar orgy followed, which
gave
Grayswandir, the two Brands and a lot of other lesser artefacts. The Castle
wand
was 0:1, but the throne gave Forever a wish - got 3 blessed scrolls of
recharging.
After wishing for a magic marker, the wand became 1:3. Another wish for a
magic
marker, and the wand remained 1:2 for the entire remaining time until the
Astral
Plane. Another throne let me genocide master mind flayers and I decided not
to
bother with ordinary MF's. Wrote a blessed ?oGenocide and used it on L, but
not
before an arch-lich gave me a lot of trouble at the Quest.

When I felt a bit more prepared I descended into Gehennom. It was quite
easy,
mostly because of the +7 Grayswandir and +5 ring of increase damage. Nothing
really presented any difficulty, but still I prepared some more before going
for
Rodney. And I'm glad I did; see beginning of post for details. Besides
getting
crowned, parying gave a lot of useful spellbooks, including cure sickness,
magic
missile and polymorph. A couple of times after praying I noticed a golden
glow,
but didn't know whaat it meant. Then I saw my max HP going up and thought
whoa,
that's a good thing. I never received additional protection, though. I
practiced
the useful spells, so I was expert in clerical and divination, and skilled
in
healing before returning to Gehennom. About that time a disenchanter showed
up and
reduced Grayswandir to +6. I never bothered to get it back to +7, even
though I
could if I had the patience.

Forever found a third magic lamp in Gehennom, blessed it and wished for a
blessed
figurine for an Archon. Fortunately, he was smart enough to go to Vlad's
tower
(with Vlad long dead and gone) before a)pplying it. Because you see, the
Archon
turned hostile and I just teleported him away and got out as quickly as I
could.
Phew, that was close...

And finally, the Priest with the Most Stupid Name arrived at the Planes.
They were surprisingly easy
and uneventful, but it was not so with the Astral Plane. Forever had to wear
an
amulet of life saving for some time, during which some lightning attack
destroyed
his +5 ring of increase damage and most of the good wands. The correct altar
was
the second, guarded by Famine. In the temple I used the two spared wishes
for two
blessed figurines of Archons. And so, Archie and Never were born. Forever
would've
stayed to get the last wish from the wand, but then Famine showed up and
made him
stunned and sick. He might have survived one way or another, but he decided
to
play it safe and offer the Amulet to Shan Lai Ching after all.

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...--More--
The voice of Shan Lai Ching booms: "Congratulations, mortal!"--More--
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"--More--
You ascend to the status of Demigod...--More--


